# score-pages -- W5-E acceptance (R-141): the skirmish score page 0xBC6 shows
# the original Score (MPScore.cpp FUN_005C92C0: kill credit = victim cost x
# (1 + rank), the survivor's bonus) sorted highest first, and the campaign
# Campaign Results page 0xBC7 draws its graph well + First / Second Place.
set render_every 300
set on_quit continue
click button "Single Player"
click button Skirmish
click start
until 90 scene == game
require scene == game
click unit 0:AMCV
key d
until 450 built(0,GACNST) == 1
# Enemy infantry walks into our start force: real kills (cost x rank credit).
cheat spawn E2 1 building 0:GACNST +3 +3
cheat spawn E2 1 building 0:GACNST +3 +4
cheat spawn E2 1 building 0:GACNST +4 +3
until 600 units_lost(1) >= 3                             @R-141:E
cheat kill_house 1
until 60 world_outcome == WON
until 300 scene == result
require scene == result
assert score(0) >= 300                                   @R-141:E
assert score_top_house == 0                              @R-141:E
shot sp01_skirmish_score
click continue
until 30 scene == "shell:Main Menu"
# Campaign: ALL01 lost -> Campaign Results with the graph.
click button "Single Player"
click button "New Campaign"
click well:allied
click button Load
until 30 scene == campaign-load
click start
until 300 scene == game
require scene == game
wait 30
cheat kill_house 0
until 900 outcome == LOST
until 300 scene == result
assert graph_rows == 4                                   @R-141:E
shot sp02_campaign_results
end
